+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+1. A single-use coupon was not given back when its order was cancelled (customer reported "already used").
+2. A customer paid €4.90 shipping on goods of exactly €50.00.
+
+## Done
+1. Cause: `Orders.cancel` passed the customer instead of the order id to `Coupons.giveBack`, which only
+   releases a coupon when the order matches. Fixed in `src/orders.ts`; test added.
+2. Not reproduced: goods of exactly €50.00 (after every discount, before VAT) ship free in the code, as the
+   README says; a test now pins it. The reported order most likely had €50.00 gross, with a volume discount or
+   coupon bringing the goods below €50.00, where shipping is correctly charged. Needs the order number to confirm.
